ORDER AUTHORIZING\nL25@P0: ISSUANCE OF WARRANT FOR ARREST OF VESSEL OR\nL26@P0: OTHER PROPERTY ............................................................................5\nL27@P0: RULE D (RD-D) - POSSESSORY, PETITORY AND PARTITION\nL28@P0: ACTIONS .......................................................................................................6\nL29@P0: D.1 (RD-D.1) RETURN DATE ......................................................................6\nL30@P0: RULE E (RE-E) - ACTIONS IN REM AND QUASI IN REM:\nL31@P0: GENERAL PROVISIONS............................................................................6\nL32@P0: E.1 (RE-E.1) ITEMIZED DEMAND FOR JUDGMENT ..............................6\nL33@P0: E.2 (83, RE-E.1) ITEMIZED DEMAND FOR SALVAGE AWARD...........6\nL34@P0-1: E.3 (RE-E.2) VERIFICATION AND PLEADINGS ......................................6LOCAL RULES - CENTRAL DISTRICT OF CALIFORNIA\nL35@P1: 12/1/18 Chapter II - ii\nL36@P1: E.4 (83-RE.3) REVIEW BY JUDICIAL OFFICER.......................................7\nL37@P1: E.5 (83-E.3) PROCESS HELD IN ABEYANCE ...........................................8\nL38@P1: E.6 (83-C.3) SERVICE BY MARSHAL REQUIRED...................................8\nL39@P1: E.7 (83) INSTRUCTIONS TO THE MARSHAL ..........................................8\nL40@P1: E.8 (83) PROPERTY IN POSSESSION OF UNITED STATES\nL41@P1: OFFICER...............................................................................................8\nL42@P1: E.9 (83-E.2) SECURITY FOR COSTS ..........................................................9\nL43@P1: E.10 (83-E.4) ADVERSARY HEARING.......................................................9\nL44@P1: E.11 (83) APPRAISAL ...................................................................................9\nL45@P1: E.12 (83) SECURITY DEPOSIT FOR ARREST OR ATTACHMENT\nL46@P1: OF VESSELS........................................................................................9\nL47@P1: E.13 (83) INTERVENOR’S CLAIMS..........................................................10\nL48@P1: E.14 (83) CUSTODY OF PROPERTY.........................................................11\nL49@P1: E.15 (83-E.9) SALE OF PROPERTY...........................................................12\nL50@P1: RULE F (RF-F) - LIMITATION OF LIABILITY.............................................15\nL51@P1: F.1 (83-F.1) SECURITY FOR COSTS.........................................................15\nL52@P1: F.2 (83) ORDER OF PROOF AT TRIAL.....................................................15\nL53@P1: RULE G (83, RG-G) – MISCELLANEOUS.......................................................15\nL54@P1: G.1 (83) DESERTING SEAMEN CASES ...................................................15\nL55@P1: G.2 (83) RATE OF PREJUDGMENT INTEREST ALLOWED .................15\nL56@P1-2: G.3 (83) ASSIGNMENT OF ACTIONS ......................................................16LOCAL RULES - CENTRAL DISTRICT OF CALIFORNIA\nL57@P2: 12/1/18 Chapter II - 1\nL58@P2: CHAPTER II\nL59@P2: RULES FOR ADMIRALTY AND MARITIME CLAIMS\nL60@P2: AND ASSET FORFEITURE ACTIONS\nL61@P2: The reference in parentheses following the local rule number is the\nL62@P2: corresponding Rule or Supplemental Rule of the Federal Rules of Civil Procedure.\nL63@P2: RULE A (RA-A) - SCOPE AND DEFINITIONS\nL64@P2: A.1 (RA-A.1) SCOPE\nL65@P2: These local rules may be referred to as “local admiralty rules.” They apply\nL66@P2: only to civil actions that are governed by Supplemental Rule A of the\nL67@P2: Supplemental Rules for Admiralty or Maritime Claims and Asset Forfeiture\nL68@P2: Actions (Supplemental Rule or Rules). All other local rules are applicable in these\nL69@P2: cases, but to the extent that another local rule is inconsistent with the applicable\nL70@P2: local admiralty rules, the local admiralty rules shall govern.\nL71@P2: A.2 (RA-A.2) OFFICERS OF THE COURT\nL72@P2: As used in the local admiralty rules, “Judicial Officer” means a United\nL73@P2: States District Judge or a United States Magistrate Judge, “Clerk of the Court”\nL74@P2: means the Clerk of the District Court and includes deputy clerks of court; and\nL75@P2: “Marshal” means the United States Marshal and includes deputy marshals.\nL76@P2: A.3 (83, RA-A.1) CITATION\nL77@P2: The local admiralty rules may be cited by the letters “LAR” and the capital\nL78@P2: letter and numbers in parentheses that appear at the beginning of each section. The\nL79@P2: capital letter is intended to associate the local admiralty rule with the Supplemental\nL80@P2: Rule that bears the same capital letter.\nL81@P2: RULE B (RB-B) - ATTACHMENT AND GARNISHMENT\nL82@P2: B.1 (83, RB-B.1) IDENTIFICATION OF STATE LAW INVOKED\nL83@P2: When the plaintiff invokes a state procedure in order to attach or garnish as\nL84@P2: permitted by the Rules or the Supplemental Rules, the process of attachment or\nL85@P2: garnishment shall identify the state law upon which the attachment or garnishment\nL86@P2-3: is based.LOCAL RULES - CENTRAL DISTRICT OF CALIFORNIA\nL87@P3: 12/1/18 Chapter II - 2\nL88@P3: B.2 (RB-B.1) AFFIDAVIT THAT DEFENDANT IS NOT FOUND\nL89@P3: WITHIN THE DISTRICT\nL90@P3: The affidavit required by Supplemental Rule B(1) to accompany the\nL91@P3: complaint shall list the efforts made by and on behalf of plaintiff to find and serve\nL92@P3: the defendant within the district. The phrase “not found within the district” in\nL93@P3: Supplemental Rule B(1) means that, in an in personam action, the defendant\nL94@P3: cannot be served with the summons and complaint as provided in F.R.Civ.P.\nL95@P3: 4(e)(2) or 4(h)(1).\nL96@P3: RULE C (RC-C) - ACTIONS IN REM: SPECIAL PROVISIONS\nL97@P3: C.1 (RC-C.1) UNDERTAKINGS IN LIEU OF ARREST\nL98@P3: If, before or after commencement of suit, plaintiff accepts any written\nL99@P3: undertaking to respond on behalf of the vessel or other property sued in return for\nL100@P3: foregoing the arrest or stipulating to the release of such vessel or other property,\nL101@P3: the undertaking shall become a defendant in place of the vessel or other property\nL102@P3: sued and be deemed referenced as the name of the vessel or other property in any\nL103@P3: pleading, order or judgment in the action referenced in the undertaking. The\nL104@P3: preceding shall apply to any such undertaking, subject to its own terms and\nL105@P3: whether or not it complies with Rule 65-2 et seq. of Chapter I of these Rules, or\nL106@P3: has been approved by a Judge or Clerk.\nL107@P3: C.2 (RC-C.2) INTANGIBLE PROPERTY\nL108@P3: The summons issued pursuant to Supplemental Rule C(3)(c) shall direct the\nL109@P3: person having control of intangible property to show cause no later than fourteen\nL110@P3: (14) days after service why the intangible property should not be delivered to the\nL111@P3: Court to abide the judgment. A judicial officer for good cause shown may lengthen\nL112@P3: or shorten the time. Service of the summons has the effect of an arrest of the\nL113@P3: intangible property and brings it within the control of the Court. Service of the\nL114@P3: summons to show cause requires a garnishee wishing to retain possession of the\nL115@P3: property to establish grounds for doing so, including specification of the measures\nL116@P3: taken to segregate and safeguard the intangible property arrested. The person who\nL117@P3: is served may deliver or pay over to the Marshal the intangible property proceeded\nL118@P3: against to the extent sufficient to satisfy the plaintiff’s claim. If such delivery or\nL119@P3: payment is made, the person served is excused from the duty to show cause. A\nL120@P3-4: person who asserts a right of possession or ownership of the property may show LOCAL RULES - CENTRAL DISTRICT OF CALIFORNIA\nL121@P4: 12/1/18 Chapter II - 3\nL122@P4: cause as provided in Supplemental Rule C(6)(a) why the property should not be\nL123@P4: delivered to the Court.\nL124@P4: C.3 (RC-C.3) NOTICE OF ACTION AND ARREST\nL125@P4: (a) Publication.\nL126@P4: The notice required by Supplemental Rule C(4) shall be published once and\nL127@P4: plaintiff’s attorney shall file a copy of the notice as it was published with the Clerk.\nL128@P4: The notice shall contain:\nL129@P4: (i) The Court, title, and number of the action;\nL130@P4: (ii) The date of the arrest;\nL131@P4: (iii) The identity of the property arrested;\nL132@P4: (iv) The name, address and telephone number of the attorney\nL133@P4: for plaintiff;\nL134@P4: (v) A statement that the claim of a person who is entitled to\nL135@P4: possession or who claims an interest pursuant to\nL136@P4: Supplemental Rule C(6)(a) must be filed with the Clerk\nL137@P4: and served on the attorney for plaintiff within fourteen\nL138@P4: (14) days after publication;\nL139@P4: (vi) A statement that an answer to the complaint must be filed\nL140@P4: and served within thirty (30) days after publication, and\nL141@P4: that otherwise, default may be entered and condemnation\nL142@P4: ordered;\nL143@P4: (vii) A statement that applications for intervention under\nL144@P4: Federal Rule 24 by persons claiming maritime liens or\nL145@P4: other interests shall be filed within the time fixed by the\nL146@P4: Court; and,\nL147@P4-5: (viii) The name, address and telephone number of the Marshal.LOCAL RULES - CENTRAL DISTRICT OF CALIFORNIA\nL148@P5: 12/1/18 Chapter II - 4\nL149@P5: (b) Filing of Proof of Publication.\nL150@P5: Plaintiff shall cause to be filed with the Clerk not later than thirty (30) days\nL151@P5: after the date of publication sworn proof of publication by or on behalf of the\nL152@P5: publisher of the newspaper in which notice was published, together with a copy of\nL153@P5: the publication or reproduction thereof.\nL154@P5: C.4 (RC-C.4) DEFAULT IN ACTION IN REM\nL155@P5: (a) Notice Required.\nL156@P5: A party seeking a default judgment in an action in rem must show that due\nL157@P5: notice of the action and arrest of the property has been given:\nL158@P5: (1) by publication as required in Local Admiralty Rule C.3;\nL159@P5: (2) by service upon the master or other person having\nL160@P5: custody of the property; and\nL161@P5: (3) by first-class mail to every other person who has not\nL162@P5: appeared in the action and is known to have an interest in\nL163@P5: the property.\nL164@P5: (b) Persons with Recorded Interest.\nL165@P5: (1) If the defendant property is a vessel documented under\nL166@P5: the laws of the United States, plaintiff must attempt to\nL167@P5: notify by first-class mail all persons named in the United\nL168@P5: States Coast Guard certificate of ownership.\nL169@P5: (2) If the defendant property is a vessel numbered as\nL170@P5: provided in the Federal Boat Safety Act, plaintiff must\nL171@P5: attempt to notify by first-class mail the persons named in\nL172@P5: the records of the issuing authority.\nL173@P5: (3) If the defendant property is of such character that there\nL174@P5: exists a governmental registry of recorded property\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nForms | Superior Court of California | County of Orange (https://www.occourts.org/forms-filing/forms)\nciteturn1132view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn822view4\",\"id\":39}); Total lines: 734\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nForms | Central District of California | United States District Court (https://www.cacd.uscourts.gov/court-procedures/forms)\nciteturn1132view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn813view0\",\"id\":73}); Total lines: 652\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFiling and Forms | United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit (https://www.ca9.uscourts.gov/filing)\nciteturn1132view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn822view1\",\"id\":4}); Total lines: 108\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFiling | United States Bankruptcy Appellate Panel for the Ninth Circuit (https://www.bap9.uscourts.gov/filing)\nciteturn1132view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn822view2\",\"id\":4}); Total lines: 114\n"
